                <pb facs="0637" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg565"/>

                <head>Inhabitants of Balgach</head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Balgach</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-07">May
                        7, 1865</date>
                </dateline>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <p>At a public meeting held in the Lutheran church, in Balgach, at half-past ten
                    o’clock in the forenoon of the 7th of May, 1865, on a motion made by C. Vulker,
                    after the close of the polls for the district election, the following resolution
                    was unanimously adopted: <pb facs="0638" n="566" xml:id="pg566"/>
                    <list>
                        <item>“The citizens of Balgach, at a meeting held on the 7th of May, 1865,
                            unanimously resolved to ratify the address of sympathy and condolence
                            from the Swiss Confederation to the American Union, and requested the
                            authorities of the canton of St. Gall to make it known to the proper
                            persons.”</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Adopted unanimously. The above abstract is correct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>S. OESCH, <hi rendition="#italic">President</hi>.</item>
                            <item>NÜNSCH, <hi rendition="#italic">Notary</hi>.</item>
                            <item>T. U. SONDEREGGER,</item>
                            <item>EDWARD WALTZLER, <hi rendition="#italic">Vote
                                counters</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
